  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   source": [
    "# Module 07: Modules, Packages & Virtualenv\n",
    "\n",
    "Learn how to organize Python code into modules and packages — essential for real ML projects.\n",
    "\n",
    "**ML Focus:**\n",
    "- Structuring ML projects as reusable packages\n",
    "- Creating modular data loading, model training, and evaluation\n",
    "- Managing dependencies for reproducible experiments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. The `__name__ == '__main__'` Guard\n",
    "\n",
    "This pattern ensures code only runs when you execute the file directly, not when you import it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a module file and demonstrate the __name__ guard\n",
    "module_code = '''\n",
    "def train_model():\n",
    "    print(\"Training the model...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate():\n",
    "    print(\"Evaluating...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if __name__ == '__main__':\n",
    "    print(\"Running as main script\")\n",
    "    train_model()\n",
    "    evaluate()\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('ml_utils.py', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(module_code)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Created ml_utils.py')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# When we import, __name__ is 'ml_utils', so the guard prevents execution\n",
    "import ml_utils\n",
    "print('\\nAfter import: the guard code did NOT run')\n",
    "print('But we can still call functions:')\n",
    "ml_utils.train_model()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. The Import System — How Python Finds Modules\n",
    "\n",
    "Python searches `sys.path` in order: current directory, PYTHONPATH, standard library, site-packages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Python module search paths:')\n",
    "for i, path in enumerate(sys.path, 1):\n",
    "    print('  ' + str(i) + '.', path)\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Note: current directory (empty string) is first')\n",
    "print('This is why local modules take precedence')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Creating a Package with `__init__.py`\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's build an ML package structure from scratch."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create package directory structure\n",
    "base = Path('ml_package')\n",
    "base.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "(base / 'data').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "(base / 'models').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create __init__.py files\n",
    "init_contents = {\n",
    "    base / '__init__.py': '''from .data.loader import load_dataset\\nfrom .models.trainer import train_model\\n''',\n",
    "    base / 'data' / '__init__.py': '''from .loader import load_dataset\\n__all__ = ['load_dataset']\\n''',\n",
    "    base / 'data' / 'loader.py': '''def load_dataset(path):\\n    print(\"Loading dataset from\", path)\\n    return [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\\n''',\n",
    "    base / 'models' / '__init__.py': '''from .trainer import train_model\\n__all__ = ['train_model']\\n''',\n",
    "    base / 'models' / 'trainer.py': '''def train_model(data):\\n    print(\"Training on\", len(data), \"samples\")\\n    return \"trained_model\"\\n''',\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for path, content in init_contents.items():\n",
    "    with open(path, 'w') as f:\n",
    "        f.write(content)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Created ml_package structure:')\n",
    "for p in sorted(base.rglob('*')):\n",
    "    print(' ', p)" 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Using the Package\n",
    "\n",
    "Once the package is created, we can import from it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import from our package\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '.')\n",
    "\n",
    "from ml_package import load_dataset, train_model\n",
    "from ml_package.data.loader import load_dataset as loader_fn\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use the package\n",
    "data = load_dataset('data.csv')\n",
    "print('Data:', data)\n",
    "\n",
    "model = train_model(data)\n",
    "print('Model:', model)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check what's exported\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('ml_package package attributes:')\n",
    "import ml_package\n",
    "print('  load_dataset:', 'load_dataset' in dir(ml_package))\n",
    "print('  train_model:', 'train_model' in dir(ml_package))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Relative vs Absolute Imports\n",
    "\n",
    "Inside a package, you can use relative imports to reference sibling modules."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a module that demonstrates relative imports\n",
    "eval_code = '''\\\n",
    "from ..data.loader import load_dataset  # go up one level, then into data\n",
    "from .trainer import train_model        # same directory\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_pipeline(path):\\n    print(\"Pipeline running...\")\\n    data = load_dataset(path)\\n    model = train_model(data)\\n    return model\\n'''\n",
    "\n",
    "eval_dir = Path('ml_package/evaluate')\n",
    "eval_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "init_file = eval_dir / '__init__.py'\n",
    "init_file.touch()\n",
    "\n",
    "pipeline_file = eval_dir / 'pipeline.py'\n",
    "with open(pipeline_file, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(eval_code)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Created ml_package/evaluate/pipeline.py with relative imports')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Relative import syntax:')\n",
    "print('  from .module import X  — same directory')\n",
    "print('  from ..module import X — parent directory')\n",
    "print('  from . import X        — current package')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. requirements.txt — Pinning Dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "For reproducible ML experiments, always pin exact or range versions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a requirements.txt for an ML project\n",
    "req_content = '''\\\n",
    "# Core ML dependencies\n",
    "numpy>=1.21.0\n",
    "pandas>=1.3.0\n",
    "scikit-learn>=1.0,<2.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Deep learning (optional)\n",
    "tensorflow~=2.9.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Utilities\n",
    "tqdm>=4.64.0\n",
    "pyyaml>=6.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Development only\n",
    "# pip install -e .[dev]\n",
    "pytest>=7.0\n",
    "black>=22.0\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('requirements.txt', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(req_content)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Created requirements.txt')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Version specifier meanings:')\n",
    "print('  >=1.21.0   — at least this version')\n",
    "print('  ==1.3.0    — exactly this version')\n",
    "print('  >=1.0,<2.0 — version range')\n",
    "print('  ~=2.9.0    — compatible release (>=2.9, <2.10)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Wheel vs Source Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "Wheels are pre-built, faster to install. Source distributions need compilation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a simple setup.py for our package\n",
    "setup_content = '''\\\n",
    "from setuptools import setup, find_packages\\n\\nsetup(\\n    name='ml_package',\\n    version='0.1.0',\\n    packages=find_packages(),\\n    install_requires=[\\n        'numpy>=1.21.0',\\n        'pandas>=1.3.0',\\n    ],\\n    entry_points={\\n        'console_scripts': [\\n            'run-pipeline=ml_package.evaluate.pipeline:run_pipeline',\\n        ],\\n    },\\n    python_requires='>=3.8',\\n)\\n'''\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('setup.py', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(setup_content)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Created setup.py')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Distribution types:')\n",
    "print('  Source dist (.tar.gz) — needs build, slower install')\n",
    "print('  Wheel (.whl)          — pre-built, faster install')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Build with: python -m build')\n",
    "print('Install with: pip install -e .  (editable mode)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key takeaways:**\n",
    "1. Use `if __name__ == '__main__':` to prevent code running on import\n",
    "2. Packages = directories with `__init__.py`\n",
    "3. `__init__.py` controls what's exported from a package\n",
    "4. Use absolute imports (clear) or relative imports (inside packages)\n",
    "5. `requirements.txt` pins dependencies for reproducibility\n",
    "6. Wheels are preferred over source distributions\n",
    "7. Structure ML projects as packages for reusability"
   ]
  }
